# Third-party reference material — not this project's to publish.
#
# `reference sources/` holds cloned third-party repositories used for protocol
# research (Flipper-ARF, ProtoPirate, RollJam, and others) plus a stray download
# archive containing unrelated SGP board projects and a commercial device APK and
# manual. None of it is authored here, so none of it is tracked. Re-fetch those
# repositories from their own upstreams if needed.
reference sources/

# The numbered engineering worklog. Most of it stays private. A measured-limits
# subset is whitelisted in tools/publish_whitelist.txt and re-included below so a
# clone of the published tree can add those files without git ignoring them.
research/*.md
!research/36_CORPUS_REGRESSION_TRIAGE.md
!research/56_315_FALSE_ELEVATED_FLOOR.md
!research/58_LATCHED_FRONTEND_STATE.md
!research/59_BAND_TILT_IS_CONFIGURATION.md
!research/79_GDO0_HARDWARE_AUDIT.md
!research/80_RA02_DIO0_LIFT_REVERSIBLE.md
!research/82_RENAULT_33US_MODEL_FALSIFIED.md
!research/86_RENAULT_RKE_CORRELATION_ATTACK.md
!research/88_SX1278_SELFJAM_MEASURED.md
!research/93_GATE_DECODER_FALSE_POSITIVES.md
!research/94_SECPLUS2_GATE_IS_NOT_THE_BLOCKER.md

# The manufacturer-key corpus file. Not shipped: it holds the same 73 keys the firmware
# already carries (masked on the published tree), so publishing it would undo the mask.
# test_keeloq_key_table.py reads it when present, or from FOBWORKS_MFCODES, and skips
# that one cross-check when it is absent.
research/sources/keeloq_mfcodes_public.txt

# Per-run harness output. The human ledger is docs/CORPUS_SCORECARD.md; regenerate
# both with tools/corpus_regression.py and tools/gen_corpus_scorecard.py.
research/sources/corpus_regression_result.json

# Kept, and read by the test suites:
#   test_frame_trim.py / test_raw_polarity.py / test_a2_reporting.py -> captures/kia/
#   test_fbk_import.py -> corpus_automotive_subghz/ and a2_kia_v34.py
#   docs/LIMITATIONS.md, docs/PUBLISHING.md, docs/CORPUS_SCORECARD.md

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Arduino build output
build/
*.bin
*.elf

# Editor
*.swp
*~

# Local secrets, if any are ever created (device credentials live in NVS, not here)
*.pem
*.key

# Bench artifacts: the card prints its per-device access code on boot over USB
# serial. Never commit it, and never commit raw bench logs that may quote it.
bench_token.txt
bench_*.log
*.bak
__pycache__/
